            <ArticleTitle>[Various aspects of drug therapy of chronic forms of ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Experience in the treatment of over 500 chronic coronary patients with various anti-anginal drugs or their combinations is summarized. Controlled (double blind) and open studies and acute pharmacologic tests demonstrated comparative efficacy of depot-nitrates, beta-blockers, oxyfedrine, cordaron, lidoflazinum, molsidamine (corvaton). The effects on exercise tolerance (bicycle ergometry) with isolated and combined use of the drugs are described. Indications for surgery are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
